# --- standalone-repo rules: when this folder is pushed as its own
# --- repository (github.com/open-pdf-edit/OpenPdfEdit), the monorepo's
# --- top-level .gitignore isn't there, so its needed rules are repeated
# --- here. In the monorepo these are harmless duplicates. Note dist/ is
# --- deliberately NOT ignored globally: vendor/openapps/*/dist (prebuilt
# --- @openapps packages) and apps/extension/openpdfedit-dist.zip (the
# --- ready-to-load artifact) are tracked on purpose; build outputs are
# --- ignored per-path instead.
/target
node_modules/
.DS_Store
apps/extension/dist/
apps/desktop/build/
.svelte-kit/
apps/extension/test-results/
apps/extension/playwright-report/

# Downloaded PDFium binaries — native (fetched by scripts/fetch-pdfium.sh;
# ~10MB per platform) and WASM (fetched by scripts/fetch-pdfium-wasm.sh into
# .vendor/pdfium-wasm/; ~22MB). Neither is something to commit. This one
# pattern covers both, since they're both under .vendor/. Top-level
# .gitignore already covers /target, node_modules/, dist/, .DS_Store for
# this subtree.
.vendor/

# Tauri build output
apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen/
apps/desktop/src-tauri/target/

# license signing keys — never commit
*.ed25519
license-signing-key*

# generated test corpus (fetched by scripts/fetch-test-corpus.sh)
testdata/corpus/*
!testdata/corpus/.gitkeep

# wasm-bindgen output for the browser extension — regenerated by
# apps/extension/scripts/build-wasm.sh. The top-level .gitignore has a
# same-looking rule, but that pattern's interior slash anchors it to the
# repo root, so it never actually matches this nested path (confirmed via
# `git check-ignore -v` — no match for either this crate's or
# openscreenshot's equivalent). This line, anchored to this .gitignore's
# own directory (openpdfedit/), is what actually excludes it here.
apps/extension/src/wasm-gen/
